AVONET trait data
-----------------

Bundled objects: avonet300 and avonet_full.

These objects contain subsets and transformations of AVONET. The AVONET
article and data are released under a Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY)
licence. Users must retain attribution to the original authors.

Source and citation:

Tobias JA et al. (2022). AVONET: morphological, ecological and geographical
data for all birds. Ecology Letters 25:581-597.
doi:10.1111/ele.13898

Data archive: https://figshare.com/s/b990722d72a26b5bfead

Example bird phylogenies
------------------------

Bundled objects: tree300, trees300, and tree_full.

These objects are pruned derivatives of tree_bird_n100, distributed by the
megatrees 1.0.0 R package under the MIT licence. The exact upstream release
asset has SHA-256 digest
71f6f712bf4c57c14570644f447c1e2eb0d76436a88075560afd4e85be1fcb78.
The underlying posterior tree sample is from the BirdTree Hackett backbone.

Source and citation:

Jetz W, Thomas GH, Joy JB, Hartmann K, Mooers AO (2012). The global diversity
of birds in space and time. Nature 491:444-448.
doi:10.1038/nature11631

Upstream package: https://github.com/daijiang/megatrees
Release asset: https://github.com/daijiang/megatrees/releases/tag/large_multiPhylo
